# Corpus raw output (large, regenerable)
# ...except the one text that is NOT regenerable. Every other raw comes back
# from scripts/acquire.py against a URL. apocryphon-of-john is extracted by
# scripts/pdf_synoptic_extract.py from a local PDF (Zinner/Mattison synoptic,
# public-domain dedication on page 1 — see sources/manifest.toml), so without
# that PDF on disk the text cannot be re-chunked at all. Committing the
# extracted witness is what makes the corpus reproducible from a clean
# checkout (todo:0888eb07, where its absence cost a carve-out).
#
# Only the manifested witness. BG 8502 and Codex III are extracted too but
# deliberately unmanifested — near-duplicate recensions would put
# near-identical chunks into chunk_embeddings and have propose_edges draw
# PARALLELS between the text and itself. See
# docs/ingest/decisions/apocryphon-of-john.md.
# Excluding raw/* rather than raw/ is load-bearing: git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so a negation under `raw/` can never re-include
# anything. Each level has to be opened before the next is re-excluded.
raw/*
!raw/gnosticism/
raw/gnosticism/*
!raw/gnosticism/apocryphon-of-john.txt
!raw/gnosticism/apocryphon-of-john.meta.toml
data/
export/
logs/
guru.db

